### Purpose: Based on testplan create a Testrun and qas file
### 1. Login kiwi  
### 2. Get testplan information
### 3. Get testcase ID in the testplan
### 4. Get each testcase  information
### 5. Based on category & is_automated choose testcase 
#### 5-1. category param: RAT, FAST, TOFT, FET, UI, ALL *combine with ";" (e.g., RAT;UI) 2. is_automated param: True, False, ALL
### 6. Based on priority parameter sort testcase
### 7. Create a testrun and get testrun information into conf/autokiwi.conf 
### 8. Add testcase into testrun
### 9. Create a qas file named autokiwi.qas
### 10. Logout kiwi


start

### Step 1.
set								autokiwi		login

### Step 2.
$testplan_info$=get				autokiwi		testplan						#testplan_id#=481

### Step 3.
$testcase_list$=get				autokiwi		testplan_case_id				#testplan_info#=$testplan_info$

### Step 4.
$testcase_info$=get				autokiwi		testcase_info					#testcase_id_list#=$testcase_list$

### Step 5.
$remained_testcase$=get			autokiwi		testcase_filter					#testcase_info#=$testcase_info$,#category#=IoE_suite,#is_automated#=True

### Step 6.
$sorted_testcase$=get			autokiwi		testcase_sort					#remained_testcase_info#=$remained_testcase$

### Step 7.
create							autokiwi		testrun							#testplan_info#=$testplan_info$

### Step 8.
add								autokiwi		testrun_case					#remained_testcase#=$sorted_testcase$

### Step 9.
create							autokiwi		qas								#testplan_info#=$testplan_info$,#remained_testcase#=$sorted_testcase$

### Step 10.
set								autokiwi		logout
